statement:
Let $\Lambda$ be a commutative ring and let

$$
 \begin{array}{ccc}
 X'&\xrightarrow{g'}&X\\
 f'\downarrow&&\downarrow f\\
 Y'&\xrightarrow{g}&Y
 \end{array}
$$

be a cartesian square of schemes [def-weil-pbc-cartesian-square]. For a scheme $T$ write $\operatorname{For}:\Mod(T_{\Et},\Lambda)\to\Ab(T_{\Et})$ for the functor forgetting the $\Lambda$-module structure [def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves]; it is exact, so applying it termwise gives a functor $\operatorname{For}:\Dplus(T_{\Et},\Lambda)\to\Dplus(T_{\Et})$ [def-weil-pbc-derived-categories] with $\mathcal H^i(\operatorname{For}K)=\operatorname{For}\mathcal H^i(K)$. Then:

1. for every morphism $u$ among $f,f',g,g'$, the inverse image of $\Lambda$-module sheaves (the inverse image of [def-weil-pbc-inverse-image], using $u^{-1}\underline\Lambda=\underline\Lambda$) satisfies $\operatorname{For}\circ u^{-1}=u^{-1}\circ\operatorname{For}$;
2. for $u\in\{f,f'\}$ and $K\in\Dplus(\text{source},\Lambda)$ there is a canonical isomorphism $\operatorname{For}(Ru_*K)\xrightarrow{\sim}Ru_*(\operatorname{For}K)$ in $\Dplus(\text{target}_{\Et})$, natural in $K$, where on the left $Ru_*$ is computed with K-injective resolutions of complexes of $\Lambda$-module sheaves and on the right with K-injective resolutions of complexes of abelian sheaves [def-weil-pbc-direct-image];
3. for $K\in\Dplus(X_{\Et},\Lambda)$, let $\Ex^\Lambda_{\square,K}:g^{-1}Rf_*K\to Rf'_*g'^{-1}K$ be the derived exchange morphism of [def-weil-pbc-derived-exchange] formed in the derived categories of $\Lambda$-module sheaves (the adjoint mate of $g'^{-1}\varepsilon_f\circ\theta_\square$ for the $\Lambda$-linear adjunctions). Under the identifications (1) and (2), $\operatorname{For}(\Ex^\Lambda_{\square,K})$ equals the derived exchange morphism $\Ex_{\square,\operatorname{For}K}$ of abelian sheaves.

In particular $\Ex^\Lambda_{\square,K}$ is an isomorphism if and only if $\Ex_{\square,\operatorname{For}K}$ is.
